 "notes": "Curve labelled 'EW' in the left panel of figure 6: 95% CL upper bound on the Yukawa strength |alpha~| vs range lambda for a vector coupled to q~=B-L, from the lab-fixed Be-Ti and Be-Al torsion-balance results (table 3). Extracted from the vector paths of WEP_figure6.eps (axis calibration from tick marks: x decades 1e-2..1e13 m, y decades 1e-11..1e-5). Converted with eq. (4): alpha~ = g^2/(4 pi G u^2), i.e. g_BL = u*sqrt(4 pi G alpha~) with u=0.9314941 GeV, G=6.70883e-39 GeV^-2, and m = 1.9732698e-7 eV*m / lambda. Plateau alpha~=1.68e-11 (g_BL=1.11e-24) for lambda >~ 1e7 m up to the figure edge at 1e13 m (mass 1.97e-20 eV); short-range end cut by the figure frame at lambda~0.26 m (mass 7.6e-7 eV, alpha~=2e-5). Bump near lambda~1e5-4e5 m from the Juan de Fuca subduction-zone geology is included. No DM density assumption (laboratory fifth-force limit).",
